<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tassilo III of Bavaria</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 741–c. 796</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a> · Also known as Tassilo III, Duke of Bavaria</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tassilo III of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a> was the last Agilolfing duke of Bavaria, ruling from 748 under Frankish overlordship. He founded monasteries such as Kremsmünster, subdued Carantania around 772 and acted almost as an independent king. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne</a> accused him of breaking his oath and of plotting with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avars">Avars</a>, deposed him in 788 and confined him to a monastery, bringing Bavaria under direct Frankish rule.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tassilo-iii-of-bavaria.jpg" alt="Tassilo III of Bavaria" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: TassilokelchSchreibmayr.jpg: Own photography by Andreas Püttmann, Original uploader was SCHREIBMAYR (=Andreas Püttman... · CC BY-SA 2.0 de · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:TassilokelchSchreibmayr-2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
